  "question": {
    "text": "Na and Mg crystallize in BCC and FCC type crystals respectively, then the number of atoms of Na and Mg present in the unit cell of their respective crystal is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TDP8m",
      "text": "\n4 and 2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Ti8wN",
      "text": "\n9 and 14\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "J2dsw",
      "text": "\n14 and 9\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4H3tj",
      "text": "\n2 and 4",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "BCC - points are at corners and one in the centre of the unit cell\nNumber of atoms per unit cell $=8 \\times \\frac{1}{8}+1=2$\nFCC - points are at the corners and also centre of the six faces of each cell\nNumber of atoms per unit cell $=8 \\times \\frac{1}{8}+6 \\times \\frac{1}{2}=4$",
    "image": null
  },
